WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.470
At our school, three teachers

2
00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:03.990
use three different agents.

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.600
One pastes pupils’ marks

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.220
into a cloud chatbot.

5
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.630
Nobody knows who approves what.

6
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.570
We need rules everyone can follow.

7
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.660
Today: writing your school’s

8
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.460
policy for AI agents.

9
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.130
A good policy answers six questions.

10
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.940
Which jobs may agents do?

11
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.260
What data may they see?

12
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.280
Who approves their actions?

13
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.280
How are they tested?

14
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.200
What records are kept?

15
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.560
And what happens when

16
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.520
something goes wrong?

17
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.740
Sort jobs by the stakes.

18
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.900
Looking things up, drafting a worksheet

19
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.520
and your own reminders are low stakes.

20
00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.590
Messages to parents and changes to

21
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.730
records need a named person’s yes.

22
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.120
Some jobs stay with people: grades,

23
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.100
discipline, decisions about a child.

24
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.100
Then data.

25
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.300
Agents see the least data a job needs;

26
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.520
pupils’ names, marks, health or family

27
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.160
details only where a rule allows.

28
00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.170
Prefer tools that keep data on the device.

29
00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.790
Laws apply, such as Kenya’s and

30
00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:18.190
Egypt’s data protection laws, and

31
00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.410
children’s data needs the most care.

32
00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.790
Cost is a fairness question too.

33
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.370
A big cloud model uses about

34
00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.270
eighteen kilobytes a request,

35
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.090
costs money and needs a signal.

36
00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.050
At twenty requests a day, that’s about

37
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.710
eleven megabytes a month per teacher.

38
00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.020
A tiny model on the phone costs one

39
00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.820
download, then works offline.

40
00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.610
Fairness also means pupils with

41
00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.430
no phone or data at home.

42
00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.410
Agent-only homework leaves them out.

43
00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.310
So anything an agent helps with must also

44
00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.510
be possible on paper, at school.

45
00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.200
Quick check!

46
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.260
A teacher wants an agent to write each

47
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.280
pupil’s end-of-term report comment.

48
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.090
Under a good policy, what happens?

49
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.090
It may draft; the teacher reads,

50
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.550
edits and signs each one.

51
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.960
Names stay out of cloud tools

52
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.620
unless a rule allows.

53
00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.850
And the teacher, not the agent, is

54
00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.810
responsible for every word.

55
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.570
Plan for mistakes before they happen.

56
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.410
Staff tell a named lead, who

57
00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.670
can switch the agent off.

58
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.100
Check the log, and tell the

59
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:33.920
families affected.

60
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.460
Fix the cause, test again,

61
00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.060
then switch it back on.

62
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.650
In the app, measure a request on

63
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.250
your phone, then switch to two G

64
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.570
and compare the cloud.

65
00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.410
Set thirty requests a day and

66
00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.430
your data price, and work out a

67
00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.650
month for the whole staff.

68
00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:53.530
Your turn.

69
00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.960
An agent sends a wrong message to parents.

70
00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.050
Who is responsible?

71
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.020
The school, through the

72
00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.200
person who approved it.

73
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.760
Remember: a policy answers six questions.

74
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.560
Keep data to the least, on the

75
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:10.560
device where you can.

76
00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.170
Count the cost, and keep a

77
00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.810
paper way for every pupil.

78
00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.190
Try it in class tomorrow: let

79
00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.970
pupils help write the policy.

80
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.500
Each group answers one of the six

81
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.380
questions, in their own words.

82
00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.230
Then take their ideas, with your

83
00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.170
colleagues’, to your head teacher.
